<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Takechi Hanpeita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1829–1865</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Takechi Hanpeita was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> and swordsman of the Tosa domain on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shikoku">Shikoku</a> who in 1861 founded the Tosa Loyalist Party, dedicated to restoring imperial rule and expelling foreigners. His followers assassinated the domain's reforming minister Yoshida Toyo in 1862, and for a time the party influenced court politics in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>. When the former lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamauchi-toyoshige">Yamauchi Toyoshige</a> turned against the loyalists, Takechi was imprisoned and ordered to commit seppuku in 1865.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/takechi-hanpeita.jpg" alt="Takechi Hanpeita" width="320" height="673" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Takechi Hanpeita · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Takechi_Zuizan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
